<article class="page">
  <header>
    <div>
      <div class="kicker">Media intelligence brief · 2 July-29 September 2026</div>
      <h1>Singapore's trade position: home coverage is about managed resilience; overseas coverage is about strategic utility</h1>
      <div class="subtitle">News coverage only · Singapore media vs US, China, Japan, India, Malaysia, Indonesia and EU/UK · English plus Chinese, Japanese, Malay, Indonesian and Hindi retrieval</div>
    </div>
    <div class="decision">Decision line: Singapore's calibrated, rules-based posture travels well, but abroad it is increasingly recast as a supply-chain and geopolitical asset rather than a defence of open trade in its own right.</div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="matrix">
      <h2>Market readout</h2>
      <table aria-label="Domestic and overseas coverage comparison">
        <colgroup>
          <col style="width:9%"><col style="width:10%"><col style="width:32%"><col style="width:21%"><col style="width:28%">
        </colgroup>
        <thead><tr><th>Market</th><th>Volume / trend</th><th>Dominant narratives</th><th>Tone + example headline</th><th>Top outlets / recurring writers</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">Singapore</td>
            <td><div class="volume">6,681</div><div class="trend">Sustained; peaks w/c 20 Jul, 24 Aug, 7 Sep.</div></td>
            <td>Tariff impact is material but contained; response must avoid wider third-country/export-control costs; FTAs, diversification and worker support are the resilience answer.</td>
            <td><span class="tone neutral">Neutral → constructive</span><a class="headline" href="https://www.businesstimes.com.sg/singapore/economy-policy/us-tariff-affects-s9-5-billion-singapores-domestic-exports-gan-kim-yong">“US tariff affects S$9.5b of Singapore exports”</a></td>
            <td>ST, CNA, Business Times, Zaobao, SBR; Low Youjin, Goh Ruoxue, Benjamin Lim, Abigail Ng, Hu Yuanwen and Li Yaning recur on policy detail.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">United States</td>
            <td><div class="volume">237</div><div class="trend">One sharp peak w/c 3 Aug; otherwise low.</div></td>
            <td>Section 301 legality and forced-labour enforcement; consumer/business cost of global tariffs; Singapore appears mainly as one economy in a 60-market action.</td>
            <td><span class="tone critical">Neutral → critical</span><a class="headline" href="https://apnews.com/article/trump-tariffs-supreme-court-forced-labor-4ea091eeee3fa1bfbe55af3f482e6bc1">“Trump imposes double-digit tariffs...”</a></td>
            <td>AP, Bloomberg/Yahoo, Reuters syndication; Paul Wiseman, Mae Anderson, Elaine Kurtenbach, Chan Ho-him and Yee Ong focus on legal architecture and costs.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">China</td>
            <td><div class="volume">n/a*</div><div class="trend">Article signal is episodic: leaders' retreat, exports, tariff reaction.</div></td>
            <td>Opposition to unilateral tariffs; Singapore as a stable ASEAN node; trade growth, connectivity and practical bilateral cooperation outweigh tariff-specific scrutiny.</td>
            <td><span class="tone positive">Neutral → positive</span><a class="headline" href="https://english.news.cn/20260917/49551c1692724e8baaa53d1d011f9acc/c.html">“Singapore's exports jump 46.2%...”</a></td>
            <td>Xinhua and Chinese-language Zaobao distribution dominate the retrieved set; Xinhua often carries an agency/editor byline (“Huaxia”), not a named correspondent.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">Japan</td>
            <td><div class="volume">n/a*</div><div class="trend">Low, event-led; no sustained tariff cycle detected.</div></td>
            <td>Strategic partnership and high-tech cooperation; Singapore as a trusted base for advanced industries; rules-based resilience rather than tariff confrontation.</td>
            <td><span class="tone positive">Neutral → positive</span><a class="headline" href="https://www.japantimes.co.jp/news/2026/07/08/japan/japan-singapore-space-cooperation/">“Japan and Singapore ink pact...”</a></td>
            <td>Japan Times/Jiji and institutional trade sources; reporting is predominantly agency-led, with few repeat named bylines in the retrieved set.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">India</td>
            <td><div class="volume">352</div><div class="trend">Dominant peak w/c 17 Aug (199).</div></td>
            <td>Singapore capital and connectivity support “Viksit Bharat”; the roundtable delivers practical pacts; semiconductors, food security, skills and digital links frame mutual gain.</td>
            <td><span class="tone positive">Positive</span><a class="headline" href="https://www.business-standard.com/amp/external-affairs-defence-security/news/india-and-singapore-ink-pacts-to-strengthen-ties-in-key-sectors-126082001157_1.html">“India and Singapore ink pacts...”</a></td>
            <td>Business Standard, PTI/Bhasha and ANI syndication; agency desks drive volume more than individual correspondents, including Hindi coverage.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">Malaysia</td>
            <td><div class="volume">3</div><div class="trend">Very low Singapore-specific follow-through.</div></td>
            <td>Comparative tariff exposure (Singapore 12.5% vs Malaysia 10%); ASEAN competitiveness; domestic Singapore reporting is largely mirrored rather than independently reframed.</td>
            <td><span class="tone neutral">Neutral</span><a class="headline" href="https://www.thestar.com.my/aseanplus/aseanplus-news/2026/07/25/trump-imposes-new-125-tariff-on-singapore-affecting-one-third-of-exports-to-us">“Trump imposes new 12.5% tariff...”</a></td>
            <td>The Star/ASEANPlus and aggregators; bylines are mostly absent or syndicated, limiting correspondent attribution.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">Indonesia</td>
            <td><div class="volume">78</div><div class="trend">Peak w/c 6 Jul (47); fades quickly.</div></td>
            <td>Concrete delivery from 26 agreements; energy, digital and food/supply-chain integration; bilateral trust and Singapore investment anchor the frame.</td>
            <td><span class="tone positive">Positive</span><a class="headline" href="https://www.antaranews.com/berita/5637460/leaders-retreat-ri-singapura-hasilkan-26-kesepakatan-ini-daftarnya">“Leaders' Retreat produced 26 agreements”</a></td>
            <td>ANTARA leads in Bahasa and English; Fathur Rochman and Aditya Ramadhan repeatedly frame outcomes as practical cooperation and strategic trust.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="market">EU / UK</td>
            <td><div class="volume">56</div><div class="trend">Small peaks w/c 27 Jul, 3 Aug and 24 Aug.</div></td>
            <td>Singapore is the working bilateral FTA template; EU-ASEAN trade is diversification/de-risking; a bloc-to-bloc deal remains desirable but institutionally difficult.</td>
            <td><span class="tone neutral">Neutral → positive</span><a class="headline" href="https://amp.dw.com/en/eu-finally-clinching-trade-deals-with-southeast-asian-states/a-79388278">“EU finally clinching trade deals...”</a></td>
            <td>DW, AP and specialist EU-ASEAN sources; David Hutt consistently takes the Europe-ASEAN architecture and China/US de-risking angle.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <aside class="side">
      <section class="panel">
        <h2>Weekly signal</h2>
